    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "4 Bedroom (1 ensuite) deceptively spacious property on the outskirts of Lifford that would make for an ideal family home. This property was suspected to have defective blockwork although following extensive testing the property has been deemed sound, a copy of the report is available upon request.\n\nPlease note this property will be offered by online auction (unless sold prior). For auction date and time please visit iamsold.ie. Vendors may decide to accept pre-auction bids so please register your interest with us to avoid disappointment.\n\nNestled in the peaceful countryside of Rossgier, this lovely four-bedroom detached property constructed in 2001, enjoys an ideal rural setting while remaining conveniently close to the many amenities of Lifford, Strabane, Letterkenny and Derry City. The property thus offers the perfect blend of tranquillity, privacy and accessibility.\n\nExternally, the property is complemented by mature gardens and hedging, generous outdoor space and ample parking, providing an ideal environment for families, or those seeking a peaceful country lifestyle. \n\nDespite its idyllic location, the property is only a short drive from Lifford town centre, where residents can avail of supermarkets, cafés, restaurants, healthcare services, sporting facilities and everyday conveniences. Strabane is also easily accessible, offering an extensive range of retail, leisure and educational amenities. Letterkenny, the commercial hub of Donegal, is only 20 minutes away, while the vibrant city of Derry is also only a short drive.\n\nFamilies are particularly well catered for, with a selection of highly regarded primary and secondary schools within easy reach, including:\n-St. Patrick`s National School, 5.2 km \n-St. Mary`s National School, 3.8 km\n-Secondary schools are available in nearby Strabane, Raphoe, and Letterkenny.\n\nEarly viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate all that this exceptional property has to offer.\n\n\nThere is a concrete step leading to partially glazed hardwood front door, accessing an entrance vestibule. The vestibule has tiled flooring and a partially glazed hardwood door leading to an entrance hallway. The entrance hallway measures at 13.1 x 7.5 ft, with carpet flooring.\n\nLiving Room: 16.6 x 13.3 ft with double aspect, and carpet flooring. There is an open fireplace with an electric fire inset, with decorative tiled cast-iron surround and granite hearth. \n\nKitchen-Dining Room: 16.5 x 14 ft, with tiled flooring, and built-in wall to base kitchen units with a tiled surround. Stainless steel double sink and drainer unit with mixer tap over. Integrated electric oven and integrated four-ring electric hob with integrated extractor hood over. Glazed double doors lead to the sunroom.\n\nSunroom: 12.3 x 10.9 ft, with tiled flooring. Tongue and grove timber ceiling, with glazed double doors leading out to the side.\n\nStaircase to the first floor.\n\nBedroom One: 16.6 x 12 ft, with carpet flooring.\nEnsuite: Tiled flooring, with fully tiled walls. White two-piece suite, and large shower cubicle with glass shower enclosure containing a Redring electric shower.\n\nBedroom Two: 11.5 x 10.7 ft, with carpet flooring.\n\nGround Floor Bedroom Three: 11.1 x 10.9 ft, with carpet flooring and built-in wardrobes.\n\nGround Floor Bedroom Four: 11.3 x 9.8 ft, with carpet flooring and a built-in wardrobe.\n\nBathroom: Tiled floor, with fully tiled walls. White three-piece suite, and a separate shower cubicle with glass shower enclosure containing an Aqualisa mains power shower.\n\nOutside: Wrought iron gates lead to a tarmac driveway, which provides ample carparking to the front. The front garden is laid to lawn, featuring mature hedging to the boundaries. To the rear of the property, there is a detached garage providing ample storage, in addition to a concrete area for additional parking. The rear garden is also laid to lawn with 6 ft high timber fencing to the rear and side boundaries. \n\nAuctioneers Comments: This property is offered for sale by online auction (unless sold prior) so please contact us early to avoid disappointment. The successful bidder is required to pay a 10% deposit and contracts are signed immediately on acceptance of a bid. Please note this property is subject to an undisclosed reserve price. Terms and conditions apply to this sale.\n\nDisclaimer - The above particulars are issued by Glen Estates on the understanding that all negotiations are conducted through them. Information contained in the brochure does not form any part of any offer or contract and is provided in good faith, for guidance only. Glen estates have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. Maps and plans are not to scale and measurements are approximate, photographs provided for guidance only. The particulars, descriptions, dimensions, references to condition, permissions or licences for use or occupation, access and any other details, such as prices, rents or any other outgoings are for guidance\nonly and may be subject to change. Intending purchasers / tenants must satisfy themselves as to the accuracy of details provided to them either verbally or as part of this brochure. Neither Glen Estates or any of its employees have any authority to make or give any representation or warranty in respect of this property.\n"
      },
